1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,936
Hamburgers, egg pancakes, sizzling noodles

2
00:00:02,936 --> 00:00:05,806
Rice balls, toast, and savory soy milk

3
00:00:05,806 --> 00:00:09,076
There are so many delicious breakfasts
around the world

4
00:00:09,076 --> 00:00:12,346
I'm going to collect them all in my
breakfast truck

5
00:00:13,614 --> 00:00:14,281
And so,

6
00:00:14,281 --> 00:00:16,083
Beelu, who loves breakfast,

7
00:00:16,083 --> 00:00:18,752
set off on an adventure to collect

8
00:00:18,752 --> 00:00:20,354
all kinds of breakfast!

9
00:00:55,656 --> 00:00:58,058
That was fun!

10
00:00:59,993 --> 00:01:02,129
Let's find breakfast!

11
00:01:02,129 --> 00:01:04,865
Good morning, Beelu! Good morning, kids!

12
00:01:04,865 --> 00:01:08,001
Today's breakfast is soy milk

13
00:01:08,001 --> 00:01:10,003
In the adventure story coming up,

14
00:01:10,003 --> 00:01:12,406
there will be three soy milk stickers

15
00:01:12,406 --> 00:01:13,874
Help Beelu

16
00:01:13,874 --> 00:01:16,143
find where they are!

17
00:01:16,143 --> 00:01:18,412
Let's collect today's breakfast!

18
00:01:21,815 --> 00:01:25,218
Circle your left hand, circle your right hand

19
00:01:25,218 --> 00:01:27,087
Clap! Clap!

20
00:01:27,087 --> 00:01:29,423
What should we have for breakfast today?

21
00:01:30,223 --> 00:01:34,094
Move your left brain, move your right
brain

22
00:01:36,830 --> 00:01:39,900
Wow, I smell soy milk!

23
00:01:41,835 --> 00:01:44,504
Let's have soy milk for breakfast today

24
00:01:53,580 --> 00:01:56,116
So delicious!

25
00:01:56,917 --> 00:01:59,319
Boss, your soy milk is delicious

26
00:01:59,319 --> 00:02:01,388
I'll take this whole bucket home

27
00:02:03,924 --> 00:02:05,859
Oh, my precious soybeans!

28
00:02:05,859 --> 00:02:08,195
You really can make the world's best soy
milk

29
00:02:08,195 --> 00:02:08,862
You're amazing

30
00:02:17,137 --> 00:02:17,938
Morning!

31
00:02:17,938 --> 00:02:19,539
I'm Grandpa Donkey

32
00:02:19,539 --> 00:02:22,009
Are you here for soy milk too?

33
00:02:22,009 --> 00:02:22,209
That's right

34
00:02:22,342 --> 00:02:22,809
That's right

35
00:02:22,809 --> 00:02:24,344
My name is Beelu

36
00:02:24,344 --> 00:02:26,947
I came from a place far, far away

37
00:02:26,947 --> 00:02:30,083
I could smell something delicious here

38
00:02:31,418 --> 00:02:33,353
What an amazing nose you have!

39
00:02:34,154 --> 00:02:35,489
Not really

40
00:02:36,356 --> 00:02:39,226
But the last bucket of soy milk today

41
00:02:39,226 --> 00:02:40,827
just sold out

42
00:02:41,361 --> 00:02:43,230
Sold out?

43
00:02:43,230 --> 00:02:44,631
Yes, it's all gone

44
00:02:45,632 --> 00:02:47,034
Those of you in the back,

45
00:02:47,034 --> 00:02:49,503
we're out of soy milk for today

46
00:02:50,037 --> 00:02:51,772
It sold out so early?

47
00:02:53,840 --> 00:02:55,242
But, Grandpa,

48
00:02:55,242 --> 00:02:57,644
why don't you use the soybeans you have

49
00:02:57,644 --> 00:02:59,713
and make more soy milk?

50
00:03:00,247 --> 00:03:03,250
Well, I still have my precious soybeans,

51
00:03:03,250 --> 00:03:04,651
but without water,

52
00:03:04,651 --> 00:03:06,787
I can't make soy milk

53
00:03:06,787 --> 00:03:08,321
No water?

54
00:03:10,257 --> 00:03:12,793
But water comes out when you turn on the
tap

55
00:03:14,394 --> 00:03:16,196
Huh? How can that be?

56
00:03:17,064 --> 00:03:19,733
Lately, I don't know why,

57
00:03:19,733 --> 00:03:23,136
the amount of water we can use keeps
shrinking

58
00:03:23,136 --> 00:03:24,337
If this continues,

59
00:03:24,337 --> 00:03:26,406
not only will I have no water to make soy
milk,

60
00:03:26,406 --> 00:03:29,810
my precious soybeans will die of thirst!

61
00:03:40,420 --> 00:03:43,090
Let's do the Breakfast Brain Workout

62
00:03:43,090 --> 00:03:45,025
and think of a way to help Grandpa!

63
00:03:47,627 --> 00:03:51,164
Circle your left hand, circle your right hand

64
00:03:51,164 --> 00:03:53,233
Clap! Clap!

65
00:03:53,233 --> 00:03:55,035
Jump up!

66
00:03:55,035 --> 00:03:58,505
Move your left brain, move your right
brain

67
00:03:58,505 --> 00:04:00,974
Clap! Clap!

68
00:04:00,974 --> 00:04:03,510
Bi Ru Akokay

69
00:04:04,444 --> 00:04:06,913
Grandpa, where did the water here

70
00:04:06,913 --> 00:04:08,648
originally come from?

71
00:04:10,250 --> 00:04:11,985
The water here

72
00:04:11,985 --> 00:04:14,654
used to come from that mountain behind us

73
00:04:15,589 --> 00:04:17,390
Then let's go to that mountain

74
00:04:17,390 --> 00:04:19,192
and see what's happening

75
00:04:19,192 --> 00:04:20,127
Okay?

76
00:04:20,127 --> 00:04:20,794
Huh?

77
00:04:44,417 --> 00:04:47,487
So the reservoir at the top of the
mountain is dry

78
00:04:50,891 --> 00:04:51,758
Hello

79
00:04:51,758 --> 00:04:52,626
Excuse me,

80
00:04:52,626 --> 00:04:55,295
why is the reservoir out of water?

81
00:04:55,829 --> 00:04:58,965
Ribbit! It hasn't rained in a long time

82
00:04:58,965 --> 00:05:00,367
That's right, ribbit

83
00:05:00,367 --> 00:05:03,170
No rain means no water

84
00:05:03,170 --> 00:05:06,239
Ribbit! Do you live on this mountain too?

85
00:05:06,239 --> 00:05:08,642
You'd better move away, too

86
00:05:08,642 --> 00:05:10,177
Move?

87
00:05:10,177 --> 00:05:11,578
That's right, ribbit

88
00:05:11,578 --> 00:05:13,847
We're moving to the next mountain over

89
00:05:15,916 --> 00:05:18,585
It rains there all year round

90
00:05:21,121 --> 00:05:24,991
But I don't want to move at all

91
00:05:24,991 --> 00:05:28,795
Ribbit! We actually wouldn't have to move

92
00:05:28,795 --> 00:05:30,197
That's right, ribbit

93
00:05:30,197 --> 00:05:33,867
Someone built a long water pipe

94
00:05:35,535 --> 00:05:38,471
to bring water here from the neighboring
mountain

95
00:05:39,272 --> 00:05:42,943
Then why are you leaving?

96
00:05:42,943 --> 00:05:46,346
Ribbit! A hippo blocked the water pipe

97
00:05:53,620 --> 00:05:56,356
So you're the big guy who caused this!

98
00:05:56,356 --> 00:05:59,226
No wonder the water can't get here from
the next mountain

99
00:06:01,761 --> 00:06:02,829
Wake up!

100
00:06:02,829 --> 00:06:03,830
Get up, I said!

101
00:06:03,830 --> 00:06:06,032
Wake up, wake up, wake up, wake up!

102
00:06:06,032 --> 00:06:07,901
Wake up!

103
00:06:08,902 --> 00:06:09,703
Get up!

104
00:06:09,703 --> 00:06:12,305
Wake up! Get up!

105
00:06:12,305 --> 00:06:14,174
Come on, wake up!

106
00:06:17,777 --> 00:06:20,247
Ribbit! Don't waste your energy

107
00:06:20,247 --> 00:06:21,715
That's right, ribbit

108
00:06:21,715 --> 00:06:24,251
He's been sleeping there for months

109
00:06:24,251 --> 00:06:27,120
Why not use your energy to move instead?

110
00:06:27,120 --> 00:06:28,588
That's right, ribbit

111
00:06:30,323 --> 00:06:31,124
No!

112
00:06:31,925 --> 00:06:34,461
I can't leave my precious soybeans behind

113
00:06:34,461 --> 00:06:35,862
and move away by myself

114
00:06:35,862 --> 00:06:38,198
I still want to make more soy milk

115
00:06:41,534 --> 00:06:42,335
Grandpa!

116
00:06:42,335 --> 00:06:45,005
Let's do the Breakfast Brain Workout

117
00:06:45,005 --> 00:06:47,007
and come up with a good idea!

118
00:06:47,007 --> 00:06:49,876
The Breakfast Brain Workout?

119
00:06:49,876 --> 00:06:50,744
That's right

120
00:06:50,744 --> 00:06:55,282
This time, everyone has to follow the
breakfast truck and dance

121
00:07:15,702 --> 00:07:17,437
It's Brain Workout Time!

122
00:07:17,437 --> 00:07:20,974
Circle your left hand, circle your right hand

123
00:07:20,974 --> 00:07:22,976
Clap! Clap!

124
00:07:22,976 --> 00:07:24,844
Jump up!

125
00:07:24,844 --> 00:07:28,381
Move your left brain, move your right
brain

126
00:07:28,381 --> 00:07:30,450
Clap! Clap!

127
00:07:30,517 --> 00:07:30,717
Jump up!

128
00:07:30,717 --> 00:07:32,252
Jump up!

129
00:07:32,252 --> 00:07:35,789
Make a sun with your hands and say good
morning

130
00:07:35,789 --> 00:07:38,124
Clap! Clap!

131
00:07:38,124 --> 00:07:40,393
Bi Ru Akokay

132
00:07:41,795 --> 00:07:42,529
Grandpa!

133
00:07:42,529 --> 00:07:44,197
I've thought of a good idea!

134
00:07:46,266 --> 00:07:49,536
First, soak the precious soybeans in water

135
00:07:49,536 --> 00:07:51,604
Then let them sit for a while

136
00:07:53,273 --> 00:07:56,743
Next, add water to the soaked soybeans and
grind them hard

137
00:07:56,743 --> 00:08:00,013
Grind, grind, grind, grind, grind!

138
00:08:00,013 --> 00:08:03,483
Wow, it's soy milk!

139
00:08:03,483 --> 00:08:06,486
Now we just need to finish the last step

140
00:08:08,288 --> 00:08:09,956
Wake up!

141
00:08:09,956 --> 00:08:13,626
Fresh, rich, delicious soy milk! Come and
get it!

142
00:08:33,847 --> 00:08:36,716
Yeah! We did it!

143
00:08:47,727 --> 00:08:50,463
My precious soybeans are back!

144
00:08:53,600 --> 00:08:56,202
So good!

145
00:08:57,804 --> 00:09:00,206
Have another bowl if you like

146
00:09:00,206 --> 00:09:01,541
No problem

147
00:09:02,409 --> 00:09:03,810
But...

148
00:09:03,810 --> 00:09:05,678
Why is this big guy

149
00:09:05,678 --> 00:09:07,680
coming back with me, too?

150
00:09:09,082 --> 00:09:12,419
Oh, you want another bowl?

151
00:09:15,889 --> 00:09:17,957
That was fun!

152
00:09:23,963 --> 00:09:25,899
Let's find breakfast!

153
00:09:25,899 --> 00:09:27,567
Here are the answers!

154
00:09:27,567 --> 00:09:30,236
Today's breakfast stickers are in these
places

155
00:09:34,307 --> 00:09:35,642
Did you find them?

156
00:09:38,711 --> 00:09:41,181
Yeah, I knew it!

157
00:09:42,982 --> 00:09:45,919
How do you make delicious soy milk?

158
00:09:45,919 --> 00:09:49,255
First, soak the soybeans in water for 8 to
12 hours

159
00:09:50,990 --> 00:09:52,525
Then drain them

160
00:09:54,794 --> 00:09:56,062
Put them into the machine

161
00:09:57,464 --> 00:09:58,331
Add water

162
00:10:00,133 --> 00:10:00,934
Grind

163
00:10:02,535 --> 00:10:03,470
Heat

164
00:10:04,737 --> 00:10:06,206
Strain out the pulp

165
00:10:07,540 --> 00:10:10,810
Finally, skim off the foam from the
surface

166
00:10:10,810 --> 00:10:12,545
And the soy milk is ready!

167
00:10:20,286 --> 00:10:22,422
It looks delicious!

168
00:10:25,358 --> 00:10:28,294
Grandpa, your precious soybeans are
amazing

169
00:10:28,294 --> 00:10:30,830
They make such delicious soy milk

170
00:10:31,898 --> 00:10:33,766
Beelu, did you know?

171
00:10:33,766 --> 00:10:34,968
Besides soy milk,

172
00:10:34,968 --> 00:10:36,302
my precious soybeans

173
00:10:36,302 --> 00:10:38,905
can be made into lots of other foods

174
00:10:40,440 --> 00:10:42,575
Just heat the soy milk

175
00:10:42,575 --> 00:10:46,246
and peel off the film that forms on top
and dry it

176
00:10:47,847 --> 00:10:49,382
It becomes tofu skin

177
00:10:50,250 --> 00:10:53,319
If you add nigari to the soy milk,

178
00:10:54,053 --> 00:10:56,055
the soy milk will coagulate

179
00:10:56,523 --> 00:10:58,992
Heat it, and it becomes tofu pudding

180
00:10:59,993 --> 00:11:01,728
Take the coagulated soy milk

181
00:11:02,729 --> 00:11:04,330
and apply a little pressure

182
00:11:05,398 --> 00:11:08,935
After removing some of the water, it
becomes tofu

183
00:11:10,003 --> 00:11:11,404
And by following the same steps,

184
00:11:11,404 --> 00:11:13,606
but changing the amount of nigari,

185
00:11:14,274 --> 00:11:16,476
you get dried tofu

186
00:11:17,410 --> 00:11:20,013
Wow, that's amazing!

187
00:11:20,013 --> 00:11:21,214
That's right

188
00:11:21,214 --> 00:11:22,549
And that's not all

189
00:11:22,549 --> 00:11:24,284
Fermented soybeans

190
00:11:24,284 --> 00:11:27,754
can become the miso in miso soup

191
00:11:27,754 --> 00:11:29,155
Through extraction,

192
00:11:29,155 --> 00:11:31,824
they can also become cooking oil

193
00:11:32,892 --> 00:11:35,895
So many things in everyday life

194
00:11:35,895 --> 00:11:38,164
are made from soybeans!

195
00:11:38,164 --> 00:11:39,165
What do you think?

196
00:11:39,165 --> 00:11:42,635
Now you know how amazing my precious
soybeans are!

197
00:11:44,571 --> 00:11:45,972
Wow!

198
00:11:45,972 --> 00:11:48,575
Grandpa, can I have another bowl?

199
00:11:49,375 --> 00:11:50,376
Of course!
